<title>USA: Cameron sees Daigle contribution $0.03-$.05.</title>
<headline>Cameron sees Daigle contribution $0.03-$.05.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cameron Ashley Building Products Inc said Wednesday it expects Bois Daigle Ltee to contribute to its bottom line $0.03 t0 $0.05 per share for the remainder of the fiscal year.</p>
<p>The company said it has completed its previously announced acquisition of the Canadian distributor of building materials headquartered in Boucherville, Quebec.</p>
<p>The company said it purchased all the outstanding shares of Daigle from its owner, Simard-Beaudry Inc.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The company said Daigle reported 1996 revenues of about U.S. $47 million.</p>
<p>The company said the Daigle acquisition increases its Canadian presence from 16 to 23 locations and completes the infrastructure of its Canadian network.</p>
</text>
